{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "Upscale video: LTX x2 (IC-LoRA Pixel Spatial Upscaler)",
    "description": "Core ComfyUI nodes only. Video upscale x2 with the distilled LTX-2.5 22B model and Lightricks' LTX-2.5 Pixel Spatial Upscaler x2 1.0 IC-LoRA, wired like vfx_clean_plate: LoraLoaderModelOnly -> GetICLoRAParameters (reference_downscale_factor 2 from the LoRA metadata) -> LTXVAddGuide(source frames, frame_idx 0, strength 1) on an empty latent at twice the source size, 8 ManualSigmas, euler_ancestral, LTXVDualCFGGuider cfg 1, LTXVCropGuides before a tiled decode. The whole clip at native fps: frames are padded to the smallest 8n+1 by holding the last frame and the output is cut back to the source count (ComfyMathExpression + ImageFromBatch). The source is fit to multiples of 32 with its longer side at most 960 (output at most 1920, multiples of 64, as the x2 guide needs). LTXVContextWindows (121-frame windows, 24 overlap) splits long clips; shorter clips run in one pass. The generated audio latent is discarded; source audio kept. LTX-2 Community License (ltx-2.x-community-license, gated on Hugging Face)."
  },
  "1": {
